# Changelog
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- `Resolver#preserve_whitespace`: when set, the extracted text is returned
  with the whitespace the handler emitted instead of being collapsed into
  single spaces. Keeps the line structure for plain text and the formats
  extracted by an external command (PDF, DOC, XLS, PPT, RTF, images); the
  zipped XML handlers join their text elements with a space and are
  unaffected. (#13)

### Changed
- Replaced `String#mb_chars`, deprecated and to be removed in Rails 8.2, with
  `unicode_normalize` and `truncate_bytes`. File handlers are now expected to
  return UTF-8: `mb_chars` used to silently retag whatever it was given, which
  is what hid the encoding bugs fixed below. Handlers shipped with this gem all
  do, a custom handler returning binary strings now raises.

### Fixed
- An extraction command exiting with a non-zero status now raises
  `Plaintext::CommandFailed`. The exit status used to be ignored, so a
  misconfigured or failing command silently yielded an empty string for every
  file of its type.
- Extracted text no longer has its non-ASCII characters replaced by question
  marks. Command output was read as ASCII-8BIT no matter what the command
  actually produced, and only the pdftotext handler was exempt, so umlauts and
  accented characters from doc, xls, ppt, rtf and image files were destroyed.
- Cutting the output at `max_plaintext_bytes` no longer corrupts the whole
  text. A byte limit routinely cuts through a multi byte character; only that
  character is replaced now instead of every non-ASCII character in the
  document, and `Resolver#text` no longer raises `ArgumentError: invalid byte
  sequence in UTF-8` in that case.
- RTF files no longer lose their accented characters. unrtf cannot be told to
  write UTF-8 — its `--text` output is always Latin-1 — so its output is
  converted rather than expected to be UTF-8.
- Extraction no longer hangs forever when unrtf writes its header but no end
  marker. Scanning for the marker did not stop at the end of the stream.
- Corrected the unrtf and tesseract example configurations, which did not match
  the defaults used by the gem.

## [0.3.7] - 2025-11-25

### Added
- Support for text/markdown content type in plaintext handler

## [0.3.6] - 2025-10-16

### Fixed
- Resolver returns nil if the handler returns nil

## [0.3.5] - 2025-10-14

### Changed
- Migrated CI from Travis to GitHub Actions

### Fixed
- Fix FrozenError when handler returns a frozen string
- Fix Object#present? not being available in tests by requiring active_support before core_exts
- Suppress tesseract extra output to reduce noise in OCR results

## [0.3.4] - 2021-04-21
- Further relax the rubyzip version requirement to allow 2.x versions
- Fix: Removed --quiet from unrtf arguments. In newer versions this seems to
  suppress the header line which we used as a marker to strip unrtf comments and
  meta data from the command output.

## [0.3.3] - 2019-10-01
- Relax rubyzip dependency. Our usage of rubyzip does not require adressing
  CVE-2019-16892 and thus is fine with 1.2, but applications using this Gem
  might use RubyZIP elsewhere too and thus will want to upgrade to >= 1.3.

## [0.3.2] - 2019-09-02
- Set minimum Nokogiri version to 1.10.4. See CVE-2019-5477.
- Fix encoding issues for PDFs.
- Bump development dependencies to bundler version 2 and
  rake version 12
- Update travis file to use ruby 2.6.4 and bundler 2.0.1

## [0.3.1] - 2019-01-16

### Added
- The max_plaintext_bytes limit introduced in 0.3.0 is now also enforced in the
  zipped XML handlers responsible for office document parsing.

## [0.3.0] - 2019-01-09

### Added
- `:max_plaintext_bytes` option to place an upper limit on the number of bytes
  returned. Also limits the amount of data that is actually read from plain text
  files and external command output to limit memory usage. Set this on the
  resolver object.

### Changed
- the unrtf handler now strips the preamble which unrtf adds to its output.
- text from external command handlers is now converted to UTF-8 before it's returned.
- the FileHandler `text` method signature has been changed by adding an options
  hash to support passing the max_plaintext_bytes limit.


## [0.2.0] - 2018-12-22

### Changed
- relaxed Nokogiri dependency to '~> 1.8' for Redmine 4 (which uses 1.9)


## [0.1.0] - 2018-02-15
- Initial release
